{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/git-diff-parser/pulls/2","id":4975465973,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVUEM2c8AAAABKI-V9Q","html_url":"https://github.com/marosoaie/git-diff-parser/pull/2","diff_url":"https://github.com/marosoaie/git-diff-parser/pull/2.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/marosoaie/git-diff-parser/pull/2.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/git-diff-parser/issues/2","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/git-diff-parser/pulls/2/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/git-diff-parser/pulls/2/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/git-diff-parser/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/git-diff-parser/issues/2/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marosoaie/git-diff-parser/statuses/ce6e916eccff315f73daff1a9b3025e250d3ab24","number":2,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Make GitDiffKit Foundation-free and add Linux CI","user":{"login":"marosoaie","id":2098985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTg5ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2098985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie","html_url":"https://github.com/marosoaie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Step 2.1 of the split plan: GitDiffKit is now Foundation-free and tested on Linux.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Library.** `Sources/` no longer imports Foundation.\n  - `consume(_: Data)` was its only Foundation use, so it is removed. **This is a breaking API change.** 0.x allows it, and `0.1.0` is to be tagged on `ce8bbbf`, before this change, so the tag keeps the old API. Callers with `Data` pass `[UInt8](data)` instead, as the `DiffParser` doc comment now says.\n  - The remaining `consume` overloads and `init()` got the doc comments they were missing.\n- **Platforms.** `platforms:` is dropped from `Package.swift`. Nothing in the library needs a newer deployment target, so it builds for iOS, tvOS, watchOS, visionOS and Mac Catalyst as well as macOS and Linux.\n- **Test support on Linux.** The tests still use Foundation.\n  - The fixture cache is `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/git-diff-parser-tests`. When that is unset, empty or relative (the XDG spec says to ignore relative paths), it is `$HOME/.cache/git-diff-parser-tests`.\n  - `$HOME` is read directly because Foundation on Linux takes the home directory from the passwd entry: `/root` in the container, while `actions/cache` expands `~` to `/github/home`.\n  - The kernel `.xz` is decompressed with `xz(1)`, because swift-corelibs-foundation has no Compression framework.\n  - `URLSession` comes from `FoundationNetworking`, and `autoreleasepool` is guarded with `#if canImport(Darwin)`.\n- **Subprocess helper.** `Subprocess` is a new helper shared by `git` and `xz`.\n  - stderr goes to a temporary file instead of an undrained pipe, which could block the child, and failures include it.\n  - `git apply --numstat` runs next to the diff with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` set, so a cache folder inside some other work tree can't make git ignore paths. The review caught this; details below.\n- **CI.**\n  - A new `linux-tests` job runs in the `swift:6.2` container. If `git` or `xz` is missing it installs `git` and `xz-utils` before checkout, so the checkout is a real clone. The image ships git but not xz. The job then runs the full suite, network oracles included.\n  - Both jobs now build with `-Xswiftc -warnings-as-errors`, so \"zero warnings\" is enforced.\n  - The Linux job caches only the fixtures, not `.build`, because the `swift:6.2` tag moves across patch releases.\n- **Docs.** README, INTERNALS.md and AGENTS.md now cover the Foundation-free rule, platform support, the Linux cache location and the Ubuntu job.\n\n## Decisions settled without the maintainer\n\n- `platforms:` is dropped rather than widened. Every platform's default minimum builds cleanly, and the tests build at SwiftPM's macOS default.\n- The `~/.cache` fallback means `$HOME/.cache` (the XDG spec's wording), and falls back to the passwd home only when `HOME` is unusable.\n- I added `-warnings-as-errors` to the existing macOS job too, since AGENTS.md treats a warning as a defect.\n- The new job is called `linux-tests`. The coordinator may want to make it a required check alongside `tests-and-lint` once branch protection exists.\n\n## Tests run\n\n| Command | Inputs | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `swift build`, `swift build -c release`, `swift build --build-tests -Xswiftc -warnings-as-errors` (macOS, clean `.build`) | — | 0 warnings |\n| `swift test` (macOS) | full suite with network: kernel 6.6→6.7, redis 7.0→7.2 and swift-argument-parser 1.0→1.5 checked against `git apply --numstat` | 43 tests in 8 suites passed |\n| `GIT_DIFF_PARSER_SKIP_NETWORK_TESTS=1 swift test` | offline subset | passed |\n| `xcodebuild test -scheme git-diff-parser -destination platform=macOS` | full suite | 43 passed, TEST SUCCEEDED |\n| `xcodebuild build -destination generic/platform=…` | iOS, tvOS, watchOS, visionOS, Mac Catalyst | all BUILD SUCCEEDED, 0 Swift warnings |\n| Local `swift:6.2` container (Ubuntu 24.04, Swift 6.2.4, aarch64): `swift build --build-tests -Xswiftc -warnings-as-errors && swift test`, with `HOME=/github/home` and no `XDG_CACHE_HOME`, as in CI | full suite, fixtures downloaded fresh, xz-decompressed, cached in `/github/home/.cache/git-diff-parser-tests` | 0 warnings; 43 passed, including all 3 numstat oracles and the kernel totals (12,057 files, 906,147 lines) |\n| Regression check: `GitNumstatTests` with the `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` fix reverted | patch cached in a subfolder of a fresh git repo | fails as expected (oracle returns no paths); passes with the fix |\n| End to end, release build, branch vs `main` (`ce8bbbf`): the same harness reads the file in 4 MiB chunks and dumps every path and range | kernel 6.6→6.7 (74 MB) | `cmp` identical (12,057 files); parse 0.090–0.094 s on both (median of 5); peak RSS 23.4 MB on both |\n| Same, flat-memory check | 6× concatenated kernel diff (443 MB) | `cmp` identical; 0.56 s on both; peak RSS 23.4 MB, flat |\n| Branch fed **1-byte chunks** vs `main` fed 4 MiB chunks | swift-argument-parser, redis, kernel | all three `cmp` identical |\n| `swiftlint lint --quiet`, `actionlint .github/workflows/ci.yml` | whole tree | no output |\n\n| GitHub Actions run 39871354494 on `ce6e916`: `tests-and-lint` (macOS) | full suite, `-warnings-as-errors`, SwiftLint | pass (52 s) |\n| GitHub Actions run 39871354494 on `ce6e916`: `linux-tests` (`swift:6.2` container, x86_64, Swift 6.2.4, git 2.43.0, xz 5.4.5) | full suite with network oracles, `-warnings-as-errors` | pass: 43 tests in 8 suites (1 m 41 s); the only warnings were apt's man-page notices while installing xz-utils |\n\n## Review\n\n`codex review --base main` failed with HTTP 400 because the configured model `gpt-6.1-sol` isn't supported with a ChatGPT account. I tried it once. The review was then done by a fresh Claude subagent given only the diff. It reported 4 findings, all fixed:\n\n1. **Medium, fixed.** Running `git apply --numstat` from the fixture's folder makes git ignore every path outside that subfolder when the folder sits inside a work tree (e.g. `XDG_CACHE_HOME=$GITHUB_WORKSPACE/.cache`, or a dotfiles repo at `~`). The oracle then reports nothing. Fixed with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`, with the regression test `GitNumstatTests`.\n2. **Medium-low, fixed.** The Linux cache key didn't include the compiler, and `swift:6.2` floats across patch releases, so a stale `.build` would be restored for good. The Linux job now caches fixtures only. The macOS job has the same flaw from before this PR; I left it unchanged and it is noted as a follow-up.\n3. **Low, fixed.** The Linux cache-location test compared the function to itself. It now checks against `$XDG_CACHE_HOME` or `$HOME/.cache` directly.\n4. **Low, fixed.** On Linux the xz download was staged in the cache folder and could be left there if the run was killed. It now goes to the temporary folder.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-22T23:22:31Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T23:26:29Z","closed_at":"2026-10-22T23:26:27Z","merged_at":"2026-10-22T23:26:27Z","merge_commit_sha":"50320a1ec1b3dde9b19d6b98e131793910c3cb3f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"marosoaie:claude/step-2-1-foundation-free-fc78ff","ref":"claude/step-2-1-foundation-free-fc78ff","repo":{"id":1430326489,"node_id":"R_kgDOVUEM2Q","name":"git-diff-parser","full_name":"marosoaie/git-diff-parser","owner":{"login":"marosoaie","id":2098985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTg5ODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2098985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie","html_url":"https://github.com/marosoaie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marosoaie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.gi